parse.tex 2>/dev/null || find . -name 'tableA6*'; cat figures/fig8_sparse.caption.tex", "shown": {"trace": {"input": [["command", "cd /hutian/paper && git pull -q --rebase origin dev; cat tables/tableA6_sparse.tex 2>/dev/null || find . -name 'tableA6*'; cat figures/fig8_sparse.caption.tex"]], "output": "```console\n% generated by figtab-repo figs/tableA6_sparse.py from sparse_subsets.csv, sparse_gap.csv, sparse_closure.csv, sparse_kstar.csv, sparse_run_info.csv; do not edit\n\\begin{table}[t]\n\\caption{Greedy A against random selection on the sparse MTEB score matrix (identity scale; models with $\\geq 30$ observed cells are tested, their observed cells split 30/70 into targets and candidates). Pool: share of observed cells (Eng 21\\,\\% is the untrimmed English matrix; test models in brackets). Gap at $k=3$: greedy A minus random in standardised RMSE with the family-bootstrap CI (FA); Rel.: the gap as a percentage of the random error (FA / pw). $C(3)$: closure for the factor model (FA) and pairwise correlation (pw); it can exceed 1, as the reference is the better of the two predictors using all candidates. $k^*$ for closure 0.9 on the grid $k\\leq 20$; ``$>20$'' means not reached.}\n\\label{tab:sparse}\n\\centering\\footnotesize\\setlength{\\tabcolsep}{3pt}\n\\begin{tabular}{@{}lcccccc@{}}\n\\toprule\n & & & \\multicolumn{2}{c}{$C(3)$, FA / pw} & \\multicolumn{2}{c}{$k^*$ (0.9), pw} \\\\\n\\cmidrule(lr){4-5}\\cmidrule(l){6-7}\nPool (test models) & Gap [CI], FA & Rel., \\% & Greedy & Random & Greedy & Random \\\\\n\\midrule\nEng 21\\,\\% (337) & $-$.067 [$-$.090, $-$.045] & 6 / 5 & 0.76 / 0.79 & 0.60 / 0.66 & 6 & 20 \\\\\nEng 30\\,\\% (332) & $-$.067 [$-$.094, $-$.044] & 6 / 5 & 0.79 / 0.79 & 0.63 / 0.65 & 8 & $>$20 \\\\\nEng 50\\,\\% (267) & $-$.058 [$-$.080, $-$.047] & 6 / 5 & 0.78 / 0.78 & 0.66 / 0.68 & 12 & 20 \\\\\nEng 70\\,\\% (215) & $-$.047 [$-$.074, $-$.018] & 7 / 7 & 0.80 / 0.80 & 0.73 / 0.74 & 8 & 15 \\\\\nAll tasks 30\\,\\% (331) & $-$.156 [$-$.205, $-$.116] & 14 / 7 & 0.75 / 0.78 & 0.35 / 0.59 & 10 & $>$20 \\\\\nAll tasks 50\\,\\% (236) & $-$.335 [$-$.629, $-$.092] & 24 / 7 & 0.72 / 0.71 & $-$0.08 / 0.55 & 20 & $>$20 \\\\\n\\bottomrule\n\\end{tabular}\n\\end{table}\nGreedy A beats random selection on the real, sparse MTEB score matrix at every density tried. Top: closure $C(k)$ (band: 95\\,\\% family-bootstrap CI, greedy A with the factor model only; it can exceed 1 as the reference is the better of two predictors). Bottom: paired gap, greedy A minus random, same predictor, 95\\,\\% CI; negative favours greedy A. Each test model is predicted on a random 30\\,\\% of its observed cells (models with fewer than 30 are not tested; identity scale). Gap at $k=3$ (factor model): $-0.067$, $-0.058$, $-0.047$ on MTEB-Eng at 30, 50, 70\\,\\% observed; $-0.156$ on all tasks at 30\\,\\%.\n\nShell cwd was reset to /hutian/repo\n```", "exit": null}}}, {"id": "befd7d37-39c5-5cf7-8dc1-41e570d77658", "at": 1795638041.9060168, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 58626, "layer": "worker", "category": "usage", "kind": "session.usage", "role": "experiment-repo", "actor": "experiment-repo", "execution_id": "84b24dfc04aed8385002df3b3b58b77e", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "usage", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "context usage"}, {"id": "208dd993-221e-5d49-a783-8f0b51ac433d", "at": 1795638041.9485786, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 58628, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.session/request_permission", "role": "experiment-repo", "actor": "experiment-repo", "execution_id": "84b24dfc04aed8385002df3b3b58b77e", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "message", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "session/request_permission"}, {"id": "6d9cdef8-f057-5619-a447-842230ea7354", "at": 1795638041.960967, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 58630, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "se